WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
Hello and welcome back to JD science.

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:07.300
Today we are exploring how substances move in and out

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:07.860
of cells.

4
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.440
In diffusion particles move from high concentration to low

5
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.340
concentration along a concentration gradient.

6
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.780
It is faster when the temperature is higher, the concentration gradient

7
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.960
is steeper or the surface area is larger.

8
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.680
Oxygen diffuses into the blood in the lungs and carbon dioxide

9
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:28.720
diffuses out.

10
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.280
Alveoli have a large surface area, a thin lining, a

11
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.220
good blood supply and ventilation.

12
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.980
Osmosis is the diffusion of water across a partially permeable

13
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:40.460
membrane.

14
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.120
Active transport moves substances against a concentration gradient

15
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.200
using energy from respiration.

16
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.540
Root hair cells use active transport to absorb mineral ions.

17
00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.980
Diffusion and osmosis are passive processes.

18
00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:58.660
They do not require the cell to supply metabolic energy.

19
00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:03.360
Active transport is different because carrier proteins move substances

20
00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:07.160
against their concentration gradient using energy, often

21
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.400
supplied by ATP.

22
00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:12.860
A useful comparison is oxygen entering cells by diffusion,

23
00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:17.560
water crossing a partially permeable membrane by osmosis and

24
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:21.060
mineral ions entering root hair cells by active transport.

25
00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:25.480
As you revise this topic, try to explain the key process in

26
00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:26.400
your own words.

27
00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:30.760
Focus on what happens, why it happens and how the structures

28
00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.700
involved help the process work.

29
00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.960
Now pause the video and try this exam style question.

30
00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:41.900
Explain why a root hair cell uses active transport to absorb mineral

31
00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:42.380
ions?

32
00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.360
Here is a model answer.

33
00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:49.740
Mineral ions are often at a lower concentration in the soil than

34
00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:53.540
in the root cell, so active transport is needed to move them

35
00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:57.380
against the concentration gradient using energy from respiration.

36
00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:01.820
If this explanation has helped, please subscribe to JD Science

37
00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:02.800
for more lessons.

38
00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.640
You can find further learning resources and practice questions at jdscience

39
00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.060
.co .uk.

40
00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:10.540
Thank you for watching.
